 set $S={...,-21,-17,-13,-9,-5,...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take ${a}_{1}=-5$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S.$*\n\n$$\n4n-9\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n…,\\,-21,\\,-17,\\,-13,\\,-9,\\,-5,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =4 \\\\  & =-17-(-21) \\\\  & =-13-(-17) \\\\  & =-9-(-13) \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  ${a}_{1}=-5,$ the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in Z$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)\\cdot d \\\\  & =-5+(n-1)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-5+4n-4 \\\\  & =4n-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={4n-9\\,:\\,n\\in Z}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-183770/field-1" "q-183770/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c5b3eb6-187f-5f16-a32e-66b0842adfe9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-183770"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-183757/field-1/d70b5c0b4a7c8109795e08b05fc75ce6c21d57f1e476c7d2aab37ba9c2c5ea00" :answer/id #uuid "66cd3892-f3f0-5705-bcb9-f2fbaf6ab7cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15+3n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183757/field-1/4d26dfc210e8238397d52649462380cb5f5f0dadb2b73f3e9036f9920a8a12f8" :answer/id #uuid "5c18f428-ce92-5add-8528-5987002c49e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15-3n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183757/field-1/7e5dca2b2a863ce6edb1890181983fa9e86d5681f739ee02d72214676ad4f1ef" :answer/id #uuid "232729b8-3106-5c55-a56c-0ce8ec695111" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183757/field-1/c4e7d998b8601b17c4147502b291b354cdc4bc99fe5df5ed329692c5749abd57" :answer/id #uuid "aa3a141c-355e-5d7e-a527-be65022c3d6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math