83765" :question/problem "Describe the set $S={...,3,6,9,12,15,...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take ${a}_{1}=3$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S.$*\n\n$$\nn+2\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n…,\\,3,\\,6,\\,9,\\,12,\\,15,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =3 \\\\  & =6-3 \\\\  & =9-6 \\\\  & =12-9 \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  ${a}_{1}=3,$ the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in Z$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)\\cdot d \\\\  & =3+(n-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3+3n-3 \\\\  & =3n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={3n\\,:\\,n\\in Z}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-183765/field-1" "q-183765/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c5b3eb6-187f-5f16-a32e-66b0842adfe9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-183765"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-183766/field-1/e88c1805fcd45ed148a6db71949a2c9f5c216ca04c8f17cf47ab2f36843d9dd1" :answer/id #uuid "345a417e-507a-5433-b915-ef5175d4932c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5n+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183766/field-1/5b1f09518ba271cdc25e4e5dd762d27091a4a23f8ea84e406fd6ed4350112cc3" :answer/id #uuid "8836f71f-9319-5638-ae89-33d65e227aa1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5n+9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183766/field-1/3a40a407a0d8e964ca9833c2c26f07a8cdb3a33ccf218eaf8f830900f419d571" :answer/id #uuid "297270af-99d1-5f36-9e1f-f76bf9240ce8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183766/field-1/186ae23e6fd33ca436ba5b6cec410b0e6493a8e3a893f40b8e077ac5c10dcafd" :answer/id #uuid "b2436ddd-c1de-5175-8635-998cf67bcb6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math 