aligned}r & =6 \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{144}{24} \\\\  & =\\frac{864}{144} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in N,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {6}^{n-1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {6}^{n}\\cdot {6}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {6}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {6}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in N}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-183795/field-1" "q-183795/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9df722a8-2db6-5bb8-a69c-b81b33037ab2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-183795"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186198771 :question/answer-fields 17592186195938] {:db/id "q-183328/field-1/ma-v1/856b99a30b32cde9ad3f794de2a0b8722e6fad17138b48d3a1d03facddb6caa0/72f9228a5e12570b0ae7a9ee713ed645b7471ad788f59b59018578886b187154" :answer/id #uuid "d63876f1-6bca-56f0-9f96-ed3512295346" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {3}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183328/field-1/ma-v1/856b99a30b32cde9ad3f794de2a0b8722e6fad17138b48d3a1d03facddb6caa0/380c2f791aca26da55c215da8f6556fd91db21d5bcf94c033d595de18b45a265" :answer/id #uuid "13720b7a-d92a-53d8-914d-33a11814d040" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\cdot {2}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183328/field-1/ma-v1/856b99a30b32cde9ad3f794de2a0b8722e6fad17138b48d3a1d03facddb6caa0/ec9f783b4818056c67fa5d6f74c04a1e69e9d9fb781222ab12e733926dfa64fb" :answer/id #uuid "a66f7219-c10b-5e9d-8453-fdae270140e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{2}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183328/field-1/ma-v1/856b99a30b32cde9ad3f794de2a0b8722e6fad17138b48d3a1d03facddb6caa0/0149046a0754709cbeccf6c6615b598814ec08919bc797d9d3c383b11deb52c2" :answer/id 