7f03fc774bf9" :question/math-academy-id "q-183779" :question/problem "Describe the set $S={…,\\frac{1}{4},1,4,16,64,...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take ${a}_{1}=4$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S.$*\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {2}^{n}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n…,\\,\\frac{1}{4},\\,1,\\,4,\\,16,\\,64,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =4 \\\\  & =\\frac{(1)}{(\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{4} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  ${a}_{1}=4,$ the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in Z$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {4}^{n-1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {4}^{n}\\cdot {4}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4}\\cdot {4}^{n} \\\\  & ={4}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={{4}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in Z}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-183779/field-1" "q-183779/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9df722a8-2db6-5bb8-a69c-b81b33037ab2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-183779"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-183689/field-1/a1f44d584f3d5c0539cb338e6289ad49d176231f52c1da87f334282351fe2472" :answer/id #uuid "d5aed1f5-51cf-59a1-b708-1651e5fc6c32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183689/field-1/5fc5100246d98d57a3a3e1d40181b00e6e8dff5d4a097ce2d7b7f6ae0b08578e" :answer/id #uuid "31ea1760-36e8-5b2a-b4be-0043d65d703c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183689/field-1/203f88d94a38bb859e78e84aea518cf34952815758cf391887040455367d62ef" :answer/id #uuid "0e8fb938-a73a-53fc-a8eb-7376e0b5ecf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "N" :db/ensure [:answer