f82f7c04e06603ef971401ed1aea6a421c38664ef5adb09f3" "q-183689/field-2/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-183689" :question/id #uuid "4a3efeb6-13c0-531b-9e5f-bba9b43b00d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-183689" :question/problem "Describe the set $S={1,2,3,…,29}$ using a conditional definition.\n\n$$\nR\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The set $S$ contains all natural numbers less than or equal to $29.$\n\nIn other words, $S$ contains all natural numbers less than $30,$ *excluding* $30.$\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as \n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,x<30}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $x\\in Z.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,0<x<30}.\n$$\n\n- We can write $x\\le 29.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,x\\le 29},\n$$\n\nor, writing $x\\in Z$ as before, we have\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:1\\le x\\le 29}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-183689/field-1" "q-183689/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f49ef1c2-06de-597c-bf4d-6d613989987e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-183689"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-183690/field-1/4d0c358832890f4f0221d2542d1721c57f92cd229eaf0a284d49f62ed4f133e3" :answer/id #uuid "890f2bef-e51e-5d86-8751-69f5e2733751" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183690/field-1/7d512723ec7933fc53d818fe067378407b0cca1985b020babe9fcffa79cfd32b" :answer/id #uuid "13683933-ad6e-5d4f-ba8c-3125838ad91e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183690/field-1/a1f44d584f3d5c0539cb338e6289ad49d176231f52c1da87f334282351fe2472" :answer/id #uuid "cd9fd1d0-643b-53f0-9efc-1d620fa11400" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183690/field-1/5fc5100246d98d57a3a3e1d40181b00e6e8dff5d4a097c