onal definition.\n\n$$\nQ\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The set $S$ contains all natural numbers greater than or equal to $5.$\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,x\\ge 5}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $x\\in Z.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:x\\ge 5}.\n$$\n\n- We can write $x>4.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,x>4},\n$$\n\nor, writing $x\\in Z$ as before, we have\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,x>4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-183663/field-1" "q-183663/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f49ef1c2-06de-597c-bf4d-6d613989987e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-183663"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181695/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "71e3d4ed-542d-5a05-ad15-08f8d9b28925" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186195343 :answer-field/correct "q-181695/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-181695/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181695/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "2e9e4337-1c4b-5742-aeb5-bea0faeb5167" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186195342 :answer-field/correct "q-181695/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-181695/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-181695"] :question/problem "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${-1,\\frac{1}{3}}$ given below.\n\n${-1,\\frac{1}{3}}={q\\in Q\\,:\\,3{q}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-1}}\n$q\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$=0}$" :question/worked-solution "The given set contains the roots $q\\in Q$ of some quadratic polynomial $p(q).$\n\nSince the quadratic polynomial has roots ${q}_{1}=-1$ and ${q}_{2}=\\frac{1}{3},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(q) & =a(q-{q}_{1})(q-{q}_{2}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (q-(-1))(q-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =3(q+1)(q-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =3({q}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}q-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =3{q}^{2}+2q-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n{-1,\\frac{1}{3}}={q\\in Q\\,:\\,3{q}^{2}+2q-1=0}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-183704/field-1/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "521fefb2-0b14-507f-bb44-d0083a076b8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183704/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "835b298a-3512-5bf9-bdf9-5f402900fb3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183704/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e38b024-f927-5fbe-a23f-6225a80f284a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-183704/field-1/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-183704/field-1/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-183704/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-183704/field-2/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "2d80faef-435b-5122-a991-6b1142c7458c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183704/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "e10e2075-12cc-5836-b34f-8b2952f49b6d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-183704/field-2/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-183704/field-2/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-183704" :question/id #uuid "4509be27-d21f-5125-bc76-908cea6d3a7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-183704" :question/problem "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${-\\frac{1}{2},3}$ given below.\n\n${-\\frac{1}{2},3}={q\\in Q\\,:\\,4{q}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$q\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$=0}$" :question/worked-solution "The given set contains the roots $q\\in Q$ of some quadratic polynomial $p(q).$\n\nSince the quadratic polynomial has roots ${q}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and ${q}_{2}=3,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(q) & =a(q-{q}_{1})(q-{q}_{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (q-(-\\frac{1}{2}))(q-3) \\\\  & =4(q+\\frac{1}{2})(q-3) \\\\  & =4({q}^{2}-\\frac{5q}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =4{q}^{2}-10q-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n{-\\frac{1}{2},3}={q\\in Q\\,:\\,4{q}^{2}-10q-6=0}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-183704/field-1" "q-183704/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad21350b-2e3b-57ee-a28c-32a7bd1b2513"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-183704"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-183751/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "1b465afd-9d4a-5e66-bb82-2ab082b159be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183751/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b8b9e96d-1083-532a-afdf-22ed86ecce03" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-183751/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer-field/choices ["q-183751/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-183751/field-2/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "68658b8a-0a26-55bc-a28c-e3c182323984" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183751/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "4ee87d01-388c-5549-80bf-d62eea91f7ff" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-183751/field-2/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer-field/choices ["q-183751/field-2/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-183751/field-3/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" :answer/id #uuid "ca877350-4c2b-561c-b85f-13a52bdafb19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183751/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7bca4b8-6e9d-530c-a2b9-634db1070508" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-183751/field-3/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" :answer-field/choices ["q-183751/field-3/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-183751" :question/id #uuid "ca280f24-6a7e-58fd-a272-82826d53c06a" :question/math-academy-id "q-183751" :question/problem "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${-3,-\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{5}}$ given below.\n\n${-3,-\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{5}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,3{x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-1}}\n${x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$x\\,-$\n{{field-3}}\n$=0}$" :question/worked-solution "The given set contains the roots $x\\in R$ of some cubic polynomial $p(x).$\n\nSince the cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-3,$ ${x}_{2}=-\\sqrt{5},$ and ${x}_{3}=\\sqrt{5},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =(3)(x-(-3))(x-(-\\sqrt{5}))(x-\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =3(x+3)(x+\\sqrt{5})(x-\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =3(x+3)({x}^{2}-\\sqrt{5}x+\\sqrt{5}x-(\\sqrt{5})^{2}) \\\\  & =3(x+3)({x}^{2}-5) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-5x+3{x}^{2}-15) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}-15x-45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as\n\n$$\n{-3,-\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{5}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,3{x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}-15x-45=0}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-183751/field-1" "q-183751/field-2" "q-183751/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad21350b-2e3b-57ee-a28c-32a7bd1b2513"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-183751"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-183730/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "d2e9e17d-2d3a-5e15-ab95-284b1328122e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183730/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "001ff48a-3989-5c87-97ae-60eac749efe8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183730/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "48d3fdb6-e1f0-53ac-a3c4-40e619bb91ba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-183730/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-183730/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-183730/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-183730/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "67816c09-8f15-5905-9f04-0e8b8ec17417" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183730/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "e39e029e-f164-5184-b659-77ae1ea78ea8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-183730/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-183730/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-183730" :question/id #uuid "e664c297-43fd-52bd-9883-9fa0a5d813f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-183730" :question/problem "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${1\\pm \\text{i}}$ given below.\n\n${1\\pm \\text{i}}={z\\in C\\,:\\,2{z}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$z\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$=0}$" :question/worked-solution "The given set contains the roots $z\\in C$ of some quadratic polynomial $p(z).$\n\nSince the quadratic polynomial has roots ${z}_{1}=1-\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=1+\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(z) & =a(z-{z}_{1})(z-{z}_{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (z-(1-\\text{i}))(z-(1+\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot ({z}^{2}-(1-\\text{i})z-(1+\\text{i})z+(1-\\text{i})(1+\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot ({z}^{2}-(1-\\text{i}+1+\\text{i})z+((1)^{2}-(\\text{i})^{2})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot ({z}^{2}-(2)z+(1+1)) \\\\  & =2{z}^{2}-4z+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n{1\\pm \\text{i}}={z\\in C\\,:\\,2{z}^{2}-4z+4=0}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-183730/field-1" "q-183730/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad21350b-2e3b-57ee-a28c-32a7bd1b2513"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-183730"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181608/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "1de51858-6a53-5c48-be00-c31c73a12a57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186195308 :answer-field/correct "q-181608/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer-field/choices ["q-181608/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181608/field-2/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "20d56ff6-031c-5c97-9829-c17b0fa0efa8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186195307 :answer-field/correct "q-181608/field-2/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer-field/choices ["q-181608/field-2/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-181608"] :question/problem "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${3,4}$ given below.\n\n${3,4}={n\\in Z\\,:\\,2{n}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$n\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$=0}$" :question/worked-solution "The given set contains the roots $n\\in Z$ of some quadratic polynomial $p(n).$\n\nSince the polynomial has roots ${n}_{1}=3$ and ${n}_{2}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(n) & =a(n-{n}_{1})(n-{n}_{2}) \\\\  & =2(n-3)(n-4) \\\\  & =2({n}^{2}-7n+12) \\\\  & =2{n}^{2}-14n+24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n{3,4}={n\\in Z\\,:\\,2{n}^{2}-14n+24=0}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-13186"] :question/problem "Describe the set $S=\\{... , -5, -3, -1, 1, 3, ...\\}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take $a_1 = 1$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S.$*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n\\ldots, \\quad -5, \\quad -3, \\quad -1, \\quad 1, \\quad 3, \\quad \\ldots\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =2 \\\\  & =-3-(-5) \\\\  & =-1-(-3) \\\\  & =1-(-1) \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  $a_1=1,$ the $n$th term $a_n$ of our sequence for $n\\in\\mathbb{Z}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)\\cdot d \\\\  & =1+(n-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =1+2n-2 \\\\  & =2n-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS = \\big\\{2n-1 \\: : \\: n \\in \\mathbb{Z}\\big\\}\n$$\n\n**Watch Out!** \n\nThe constructive definition of a set is typically not unique. \n\nSince the elements of $A$ are generated by a *two-way* infinite arithmetic sequence, we could have picked *any* term in our sequence as $a_1$ when determining $a_n.$ We selected $a_1 = 1$ because this led to a nice, simple expression in our constructive definition." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-13184"] :question/problem "Describe the set $S=\\left\\{\\ldots, -36, -6, -1, -\\dfrac1{6}, -\\dfrac1{36}, ...\\right\\}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take $a_1 = -\\dfrac16$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S.$*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n\\ldots,\\quad -36, \\quad -6, \\quad -1, \\quad -\\dfrac1{6}, \\quad -\\dfrac1{36}, \\quad \\ldots\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=\\dfrac16{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =(\\frac{-6}{-36}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-1}{-6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{6})}{(-1)} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  $a_1=-\\dfrac16,$ the $n$th term $a_n$ of our sequence for $n\\in\\mathbb{Z}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{1}{6})\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{6})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{6})\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{6})}^{-1}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{6})}^{n} \\\\  & =-{(\\frac{1}{6})}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS = \\left\\{-\\left(\\dfrac16\\right)^{n} \\: : \\: n\\in \\mathbb{Z}\\right\\}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-13144"] :question/problem "Describe the set $S = \\{-9,-8,-7, ..., 5\\}$ using a conditional definition." :question/worked-solution "The set $S$ contains all integer numbers between $-9$ and $5$ (including $-9$ and $5$).\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS = \\{ x \\in \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\mathbb Z} \\: : \\: \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-9} \\leq x \\leq \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}5} \\}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example, we can write $S$ equivalently as follows:\n\n$$\nS = \\big\\{ x \\in \\mathbb Z \\: : \\: -10 \\lt x \\lt 6 \\big\\}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-13185"] :question/problem "Find the missing coefficients $p$ and $q$ in the conditional definition of the set given below.\n\n$$\n\\{\\pm 3\\textrm{i}\\} = \\Big\\{z \\in \\mathbb{C} \\: : \\: 4z^2+pz+q = 0 \\Big\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The given set contains the roots $z\\in\\mathbb C$ of some quadratic polynomial $f(z).$\n\nSince the quadratic polynomial has roots $z_1=-3\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2=3\\textrm{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(z) & =a(z-{z}_{1})(z-{z}_{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (z-(-3\\text{i}))(z-(3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (z+3\\text{i})(z-3\\text{i}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot ({z}^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot ({z}^{2}-9{\\text{i}}^{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot ({z}^{2}+9) \\\\  & =4{z}^{2}+36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\pm 3\\textrm{i}\\} = \\Big\\{z \\in \\mathbb{C} \\: : \\: 4z^2+\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0}z+\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}36} = 0 \\Big\\}\n$$\n\nFinally, $p=0$ and $q=36.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
